hed the RSK mainnet.","source_url":"https://rootstock.io/rsk-white-paper-updated.pdf"}],"regulatory_status":null},"narrative":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","purpose":"Extend Bitcoin into EVM-compatible smart contracts and financial applications while using BTC as the native economic asset.","positioning":"Bitcoin''s long-running EVM finance sidechain, secured by merge mining and connected to BTC through the HSM-backed PowPeg.","competitors":[{"name":"Stacks","relationship":"Bitcoin smart-contract platform competitor"},{"name":"Core","relationship":"Bitcoin-aligned EVM and DeFi competitor"},{"name":"Bitlayer","relationship":"newer Bitcoin L2 and bridge competitor"}],"narrative_arc":"Rootstock progressed from an early federated Bitcoin sidechain to merge mining above 85% of Bitcoin hash power and layered PowPeg defenses, prioritizing longevity and BTC denomination over a new gas-token flywheel.","media_sentiment":"neutral"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No chain-level designation is asserted; an archived exact-name SDN review remains an explicit gap."},"extraction_flags":["powpeg_federation","emergency_multisig","merge_mining_dependency","bridge_risk","upgrade_coordination"],"audit_status":null,"risks":[{"type":"powpeg_trust","detail":"RBTC exits depend on a threshold group of identified pegnatories, PowHSM behavior, Bridge consensus logic, and honest/available Bitcoin miners rather than Bitcoin consensus alone.","source_url":"https://ips.rootstock.io/IPs/RSKIP201.html"},{"type":"emergency_control","detail":"The adopted design includes a 3-of-4 emergency multisig behind a long timelock, trading recovery availability against additional signatory trust.","source_url":"https://ips.rootstock.io/IPs/RSKIP201.html"},{"type":"powpeg_migration","detail":"Changing PowPeg composition moves bitcoin through an irreversible process; spendability validation adds safeguards but confirms the migration is a critical boundary.","source_url":"https://ips.rootstock.io/IPs/RSKIP419.html"},{"type":"miner_dependency","detail":"Merge mining imports substantial Bitcoin hash power, but miner participation, fee economics, and censorship incentives are not equivalent to native Bitcoin settlement.","source_url":"https://dev.rootstock.io/"}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"Rootstock retained $73.6M TVL and $43.9M in 30-day DEX volume after eight years, though TVL was 74.03% below peak and tracked protocol revenue was negligible.","postmortem":null,"why":"Rootstock survives because it gives Bitcoin holders EVM functionality without inventing a volatile gas asset, uses familiar Ethereum tooling, and recruits Bitcoin miners for merge-mined security; growth remains constrained by PowPeg trust and competition from newer Bitcoin layers.","success_mechanism":"BTC is locked into RBTC, merge miners order and secure the sidechain, EVM compatibility attracts existing tooling, and layered HSM/multisig controls manage peg-outs.","strategic_choices":["Use RBTC rather than launch an independent native gas supply.","Adopt EVM/Web3 compatibility to reuse Ethereum developer tooling.","Secure block production through Bitcoin merge mining.","Layer PowHSMs, federation thresholds, timelocked emergency recovery, and spendability validation around the peg."],"unknowns":["Current pegnatory identities, threshold, geographic distribution, hardware diversity, and operational independence.","Current merge-miner concentration and the share economically committed beyond nominal hash support.","Application, bridge, and collateral concentration within the $73.6M TVL.","Why the reviewed revenue adapter reports almost no protocol revenue despite continuing fees and volume."],"lessons_learned":["Avoiding a new gas token can preserve BTC-native identity and reduce dilution.","Merge mining does not remove the separate trust model of a two-way peg.","Long operational history is evidence of resilience, not proof that bridge governance is trustless."],"could_differ":"A fully trust-minimized Bitcoin bridge would improve the core security claim, but current Bitcoin scripting cannot reproduce every PowPeg availability and recovery property without new tradeoffs.","outlook":{"bull":"Institutional Bitcoin finance and better bridges revive liquidity on a proven EVM network.","base":"Rootstock remains a durable but modest Bitcoin DeFi venue.","bear":"Users prefer newer Bitcoin layers or native protocols and PowPeg trust limits institutional adoption.","most_likely":"base"},"cause_tags":["bitcoin_sidechain","merge_mining","powpeg","rbtc","evm_compatibility"],"confidence":"high"}},"meta":{"dimension_completeness_pct":100,"data_completeness_pct":82,"confidence":"high","unsourced_fields":["capital.total_raised_usd","capital.treasury_usd","team.regulatory_status","risk.audit_status","risk.current_pegnatory_roster_and_threshold","risk.archived_sanctions_check","onchain.active_addresses_daily","onchain.dev_activity_monthly","onchain.tvl_concentration","synthesis.current_merge_miner_concentration"],"last_reviewed":"2026-07-29"}},{"chain":"Berachain","source_catalog":{"coverage":{"title":"Chaindump top-50 chain coverage snapshot","url":"https://chaindump.xyz/api/chains"},"launch":{"title":"Berachain mainnet launch support announcement","url":"https://www.okx.com/help/okx-wallet-to-support-berachain-network"},"overview":{"title":"Berachain protocol documentation","url":"https://docs.berachain.com/"},"pol":{"title":"Berachain Proof-of-Liquidity overview","url":"https://docs.berachain.com/general/proof-of-liquidity/overview"},"bera":{"title":"BERA token economics and allocation","url":"https://docs.berachain.com/general/tokens/bera"},"bgt":{"title":"BGT governance and reward token","url":"https://docs.berachain.com/general/tokens/bgt"},"beaconkit":{"title":"Berachain BeaconKit consensus architecture","url":"https://docs.berachain.com/nodes/architecture/beaconkit-consensus"},"funding":{"title":"Berachain $100M Series B 